Build the long-path prefix with backslashes only.

_win32_longpath() puts "\\?\" in front of os.path.normpath(path).
Behind that prefix Windows takes the path as it is, and only
backslashes separate there. normpath separates with os.sep, which is
"/" in MSYS2's Python while MSYSTEM is set, as it is in every MSYS2
shell, so the fixtures' copies failed with WinError 3. The prefix now
gets backslashes whatever os.sep is.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/src/pytest_datadir/plugin.py
+++ b/src/pytest_datadir/plugin.py
@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@
         # to a path string tells the Windows APIs to disable all string parsing
         # and to send the string that follows it straight to the file system".
         # (See https://docs.microsoft.com/pt-br/windows/desktop/FileIO/naming-a-file)
-        normalized = os.path.normpath(path)
+        # Behind the prefix only backslashes separate, whatever os.sep is.
+        normalized = os.path.normpath(path).replace("/", "\\")
         if not normalized.startswith("\\\\?\\"):
             is_unc = normalized.startswith("\\\\")
             # see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Path_(computing)#Universal_Naming_Convention # noqa: E501
